@startuml
' Figure 27-2: the interned set-automaton DAG for the Beta left-hand side, and the
' size-optimal quotient -- structurally-equal sub-patterns share one StateId.
skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE
skinparam defaultFontName monospaced
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam rectangle {
  BorderColor #4A5568
  FontColor #1A202C
}
skinparam ArrowColor #4A5568
top to bottom direction

title Figure 27-2 — interning the LHS App(Lam(fun), arg)\n(structurally-equal sub-patterns share one StateId)

package "LHS pattern (a nested positional pattern)" #EDF2F7 {
  rectangle "App\narity 2" as P_App #CBD5E0
  rectangle "Lam\narity 1" as P_Lam #CBD5E0
  rectangle "Var(fun)" as P_f #E2E8F0
  rectangle "Var(arg)" as P_a #E2E8F0
  P_App --> P_Lam : "child 0"
  P_App --> P_a : "child 1"
  P_Lam --> P_f : "child 0"
}

package "interned states (the tc(K) quotient)" #FDF0E0 {
  rectangle "s0 = Var(fun)" as S0 #F6C177
  rectangle "s1 = Lam[s0]" as S1 #F6C177
  rectangle "s2 = Var(arg)" as S2 #F6C177
  rectangle "<b>s3 = App[s1, s2]</b>\nentry, RootKey{App, 2}" as S3 #A7D8B6
  S3 --> S1
  S3 --> S2
  S1 --> S0
}

P_f  ..> S0 : intern
P_Lam ..> S1 : intern
P_a  ..> S2 : intern
P_App ..> S3 : intern

note bottom of S3 #FCF3D0
  An App-key embeds child StateIds, so two applications intern to one state
  iff same operator AND children already interned equal. A second occurrence
  of any sub-pattern reuses its StateId: #states <= #distinct sub-patterns,
  independent of inspection order (doc 21 section 7.2).
end note
@enduml
